a course on close relationships for about 15 years. And I started to see a lot of overlap between mean the ways people were talking about their workplace issues, the emotions that they were feeling, you know, complex things like ambivalence, loving and hating your job at the same time, trends around interviewing like ghosting and icing and these kinds of things. These same things were things that I've been teaching in the context of romantic relationships and concepts that therapists that therapists in that space have been grappling with for a really long time and helping people kind of get their head around. And I thought, why not adopt something? some of those therapeutic perspectives, some of the things that we know help people through difficulties
关于亲密关系的课程大约有 15 年了。我开始发现人们谈论职场问题的方式、他们感受到的情绪之间有很多重叠之处，你知道，比如矛盾心理这样复杂的事情——同时爱着和恨着你的工作，面试中的一些趋势比如“失踪”（ghosting）、“冷落”（icing）以及诸如此类的事情。这些同样的事情也是我一直在浪漫关系语境中教授的内容，并且是该领域的治疗师们长期以来一直在努力应对、并帮助人们理清头绪的概念。我想，为什么不把其中的一些

