in their interpersonal relationships to our relationships with our career. Now, in the book, you outline five key drivers that make people consider leaving their jobs. Can you talk briefly about those? Yes, I actually started with the toughest kind of most existential one, which is having an identity crisis at work. This idea that you can just fall out of love with something. that has been defining you for a really long time, that your core sense of who you are as a person, your identity as a human being, is very much wrapped up in your workplace identity,
治疗视角，把我们所知道的能够帮助人们度过人际关系困境的方法，应用到我们与职业的关系中去呢？在书中，你概述了导致人们考虑离职的五个关键驱动因素。你能简要谈谈这些因素吗？是的，我实际上是从最艰难、最存在主义的一种开始的，那就是在工作中经历身份危机。这种观点认为，你可能会对某个长期定义你、让你作为一个人对自己的核心认知以及作为人类的身份与职场身份紧密相连的事物，

