but you're starting to question that. And I think people who go through this are often very advanced in their careers. They've spent a lot of time and money getting there. They have a lot of status. And so kind of grappling with falling out of love with something that still defines you is a common experience among our kind of more well-seasoned career goers out there. From there, I talk about being drifted apart from your job. And this is a little bit like looking over at your spouse and thinking, who are you? You are not the person that I'm married, that I initially got into this romantic relationship with. I don't recognize you.
不知不觉就失去了爱意，但你开始对此产生怀疑。我认为经历这一过程的人通常在职业生涯中处于相当高级的阶段。他们花费了大量时间和金钱才走到这一步。他们拥有很高的地位。因此，努力去接受自己不再爱那个依然定义着自己的事物，是那些比较成熟的职场人士中一种常见的经历。在此之后，我谈到了与工作渐行渐远。这有点像看着你的配偶，然后想：你是谁？你根本不是我结婚的那个人，不是我最初开始这段浪漫关系时的那个人。我认不出你了。

