And when we go through this experience, a lot of us think that it's really the other person or in this kind of metaphor, the career that's changed. It's not so much us. And so their journey is really about understanding who's changed, you know, and how much I have changed. and often we change, not for the better or the worst, but in different ways and parallel ways. I also talk about this kind of idea of being spread too thin. And I think, you know, this chapter of the book is really for everybody, even if you're not
当我们经历这种体验时，我们中的很多人会认为真正改变的是对方，或者在这个隐喻中，是职业变了。并不是我们变了多少。所以他们的这段心路历程实际上是去理解到底是谁变了，你知道的，以及我自己变了多少。而且通常我们的改变并不是朝着更好或更坏的方向，而是朝着不同且平行的方向。我还谈到了这种“分身乏术”的想法。我认为，你知道的，书中的这一章其实适合每一个人，即使你并没有

