relationships outside of work. But, you know, is that putting too much importance on something that is basically, you know, it's giving you the money to live and work and put a roof over your head and eat food? I love this question. So the first answer is absolutely not. It is not necessary to be in love with your job. When it becomes an issue is when you are in an industry or you're working for a company that expects that level of identity commitment, where everyone who thrives there is in love with their job and they see it as a core part of who they are and you maybe don't actually have that same kind of relationship with your career, that mismatch is where things start to go awry. Or you want to be in love with your job, but you don't know how to get it. I do think that kind of the matching
工作之外的人际关系。但是，你知道，这会不会是对一件本质上只是给你提供金钱来生活、工作、遮风挡雨和买食物的东西赋予了过高的重要性？我非常喜欢这个问题。所以，第一个答案是：绝对不。爱上工作并不是必须的。当它成为一个问题时，是因为你身处一个行业，或者在一家期望那种程度的身份承诺的公司工作，在那里，所有蓬勃发展的人都热爱他们的工作，并将其视为自我核心的一部分，而你可能并没有与你的职业建立那种关系，这种不匹配才是事情开始出问题的地方。或者你想爱上你的工作，却不知道该如何做到。我确实认为那种匹配的

